{
  "methodology": "Four live Rep4 roles, no additional dealer. One fresh secret shifted table per scalar lookup. Public function tables and established seed provisioning are one-time inputs; six table-sized checked corrections recur for each lookup. All payload bytes sum the four roles and include consistency hashes. Lookup begins with secret indices already quantized into the 12-bit grid. Quantization and input range checks, input sharing, and validation output opening are excluded; the recurring total is therefore a lower bound for complete activation communication. Batch amortization divides actual recurring preprocessing plus online bytes by the lookup count, not by a future reuse count. Dense truth-table reference, not compact FSS key generation or a network-latency measurement.",
